                        "source_sense_description": "erniedrigend: Gang zu jemandem, den man demütig um Verzeihung bitten muss für etwas, was man gegen dessen Willen/gegen dessen Interessen gesagt oder getan hat",
                        "target_lang_word": "eat humble pie",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eat humble pie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0da2ceb3-3b42-36e7-9aee-2b4c2915d08a",
                                        "entry_id": "50bbad95-afd6-3a73-97ce-5b3501254e80",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To admit one's faults; to make a humiliating apology."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "685eb0d5-b190-498d-8bf5-332504c644a7",
                                                "sense_id": "0da2ceb3-3b42-36e7-9aee-2b4c2915d08a",
                                                "text": "They were good-natured enough out of their cups, and ate their humble-pie with very good appetites at a reconciliation dinner which Colonel W. had with the 44th, and where he was as perfectly stupid and correct as Prince Prettyman need be. Hang him!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fb6e5de-d726-4202-b415-d2b61bcfb1d0",
                                                "sense_id": "0da2ceb3-3b42-36e7-9aee-2b4c2915d08a",
                                                "text": "Polly had a spice of girlish malice, and rather liked to see domineering Tom eat humble-pie, just enough to do him good, you know."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e57fe74a-94e7-44d6-8baa-99808a11215a",
                                                "sense_id": "0da2ceb3-3b42-36e7-9aee-2b4c2915d08a",
                                                "text": "Angela shook her head. “Men are dull creatures.”\n“I have already granted that, and I am eating humble pie in asking for an explanation.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7eaba06c-e5ed-4796-acd6-9fe1bc184c73",
                                                "sense_id": "0da2ceb3-3b42-36e7-9aee-2b4c2915d08a",
                                                "text": "You square the G.V., and go home before you have to. That’s my advice. If you don’t eat humble-pie now you may live to fare worse later."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eddd74b8-eb18-4642-ac01-453623652048",
                                                "sense_id": "0da2ceb3-3b42-36e7-9aee-2b4c2915d08a",
                                                "text": "But there seems little doubt that Fukuyama has had to eat rather a lot of humble pie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d3faa83-27cc-42df-8691-ba24cec609c6",
                                                "sense_id": "0da2ceb3-3b42-36e7-9aee-2b4c2915d08a",
                                                "text": "Should the economists who sounded the alarm — the same people who got so many high-profile predictions wrong in recent years — be sitting down to eat another course of humble pie? Well, it’s not that simple."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
